WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.222 --> 00:00:01.196
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.196 --> 00:00:02.029
It's Evan.

00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:03.466
My one word is believe.

00:00:03.466 --> 00:00:06.224
And I believe in people more
than they believe in themselves

00:00:06.224 --> 00:00:09.021
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:09.021 --> 00:00:12.379
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.571
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:13.571 --> 00:00:16.705
today's message is live in the moment.

00:00:16.705 --> 00:00:18.622
Over to you, Conor McGregor.

00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:20.428
(rooster crows)

00:00:20.428 --> 00:00:23.489
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.089
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:30.249
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:32.215
- I don't like to think too far ahead.

00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:33.404
- [Interviewer] So, you haven't
thought alternative careers?

00:00:33.404 --> 00:00:34.616
- No, I don't like thinking too far ahead.

00:00:34.616 --> 00:00:37.489
People set, like, goals,
long-distance goals.

00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:39.162
That's too much for me.

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:42.252
I already feel like I'm livin'
it and then I just carry on,

00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:43.085
doing that.

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:44.069
You know, carry on day by day,

00:00:44.069 --> 00:00:46.513
already living the final goal,

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:47.770
the goal of being the world champion.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.891
I already carry myself like
I'm the world champion.

00:00:49.891 --> 00:00:52.016
I already speak like I'm a world champion

00:00:52.016 --> 00:00:53.114
and that's it.

00:00:53.114 --> 00:00:56.463
I just carry on, day by day,
so I'll take it as it comes.

00:00:56.463 --> 00:01:00.034
Again, like you said, you were
asking me about the future,

00:01:00.034 --> 00:01:03.072
I'll let you know a little bit
closer, you know what I mean?

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:05.247
All I can see right now is the gold.

00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:06.319
That's all I can see.

00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:09.345
- I don't put much faith in
five-year or 10-year plans.

00:01:09.345 --> 00:01:10.993
It's one of the most common
questions I get asked,

00:01:10.993 --> 00:01:11.862
when I do interviews.

00:01:11.862 --> 00:01:13.113
"What are you going to do in five years?

00:01:13.113 --> 00:01:15.556
Where do you see your YouTube
channel being in five years

00:01:15.556 --> 00:01:16.543
or 10 years?"

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.376
I have no idea.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.057
I don't know if I'll still be
doing YouTube in five years

00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:20.322
or ten years.

00:01:20.322 --> 00:01:23.674
I think what's really important
is that you have a mission

00:01:23.674 --> 00:01:24.996
of something you're trying to accomplish,

00:01:24.996 --> 00:01:27.659
a general direction that you
want to go, and some big goal

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:30.714
that you're trying to reach,
but then not be so attached

00:01:30.714 --> 00:01:32.996
to how you're going to
go out and accomplish it

00:01:32.996 --> 00:01:35.103
and so, I want to help
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:01:35.103 --> 00:01:37.268
Conor McGregor, I want us to
win the world championship,

00:01:37.268 --> 00:01:38.101
great.

00:01:38.101 --> 00:01:39.630
I want to help a billion entrepreneurs.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:42.096
How I get there doesn't matter, right?

00:01:42.096 --> 00:01:44.918
I've got to do something that
I enjoy, that I have fun doing,

00:01:44.918 --> 00:01:46.669
that I feel is having a big impact,

00:01:46.669 --> 00:01:48.928
but, the specifics doesn't matter.

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:51.914
And so, I know my long
term of where I'm going

00:01:51.914 --> 00:01:54.739
and then I know what I'm
working on right now.

00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:56.242
You know, at the end of
the year, I want to try

00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:58.210
to have a million subscribers.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.101
Every week, I'm creating
content, making videos,

00:02:01.101 --> 00:02:04.867
for you guys and I make kind
of minor changes along the way

00:02:04.867 --> 00:02:07.114
and introduce new things and new ideas.

00:02:07.114 --> 00:02:10.202
But am I still going to be
on YouTube in five years?

00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:11.549
I don't know.

00:02:11.549 --> 00:02:13.602
What am I going to be doing
in five years or 10 years?

00:02:13.602 --> 00:02:15.467
I'm going to be doing something awesome,

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.152
to help reach a billion entrepreneurs.

00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:18.476
That's what I'm going to be doing.

00:02:18.476 --> 00:02:20.000
That's what motivates me.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.882
And so I think it's great
to have plans, right?

00:02:22.882 --> 00:02:23.734
Planning is great.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.512
It's not that you don't
want to have any plans.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.673
You don't want to have any goals.

00:02:26.673 --> 00:02:29.181
You want to just wake
up and see what happens,

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:30.645
'cause most people don't just wake up

00:02:30.645 --> 00:02:32.391
and do something amazing.

00:02:32.391 --> 00:02:33.625
You know, having some kind of plan,

00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:34.987
having some kind of structure,

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:38.335
helps you on the days when
you're not really motivated.

00:02:38.335 --> 00:02:39.168
This is important.

00:02:39.168 --> 00:02:43.393
Whenever I feel like what
I'm doing is out of whack,

00:02:43.393 --> 00:02:46.896
doesn't feel right anymore, I'm
yearning for something else,

00:02:46.896 --> 00:02:49.868
you know, you get that little
frustration bubbling up

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.097
that I want to add something else in

00:02:52.097 --> 00:02:54.526
and my current schedule
doesn't allow for it.

00:02:54.526 --> 00:02:55.985
Whenever I feel like that,

00:02:55.985 --> 00:02:57.546
then I have to re-jig my schedule.

00:02:57.546 --> 00:03:00.819
I've got to figure out, okay,
what no longer serves me

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:03.397
and what am I yearning for
and how can I put that in?

00:03:03.397 --> 00:03:05.060
And I can't plan for that.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:05.976
That's the challenge.

00:03:05.976 --> 00:03:07.505
You don't know what kind of
person you're going to be

00:03:07.505 --> 00:03:09.748
in five years or 10 years or
what's going to interest you

00:03:09.748 --> 00:03:11.497
or the new things that have come out.

00:03:11.497 --> 00:03:15.098
You know, 10 years ago, YouTube
wasn't even a big thing.

00:03:15.098 --> 00:03:17.215
If it was I want to help
a billion entrepreneurs,

00:03:17.215 --> 00:03:19.270
I'm going to do that
by getting on MySpace,

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.603
which was all the rage 10 years ago.

00:03:21.603 --> 00:03:25.777
Then, who cares if I'm the
number one MySpacer right now?

00:03:25.777 --> 00:03:26.927
It's not going to help me achieve my goal

00:03:26.927 --> 00:03:28.639
of helping a billion entrepreneurs.

00:03:28.639 --> 00:03:30.537
And so I think having a specific target

00:03:30.537 --> 00:03:32.014
can really be helpful,

00:03:32.014 --> 00:03:34.296
in terms of you accomplishing that target,

00:03:34.296 --> 00:03:37.859
but it doesn't mean that that's
actually going to help you

00:03:37.859 --> 00:03:39.986
with your long-term goals.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.370
And so, I'd be stubborn
about the big thing

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:43.970
that you're trying to
accomplish, but be flexible

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:45.272
in the how.

00:03:45.272 --> 00:03:46.623
The other thing that I
have a really hard time,

00:03:46.623 --> 00:03:50.915
and maybe this is for you guys
too, is whenever I set a goal

00:03:50.915 --> 00:03:53.463
that might be multi-years out,

00:03:53.463 --> 00:03:56.379
I initially, immediately
already want to think of how

00:03:56.379 --> 00:03:57.752
to accomplish that right now.

00:03:57.752 --> 00:03:59.572
I would look at a five-year
goal and say how do I do that

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.671
in five months.

00:04:00.671 --> 00:04:02.399
How do I get that happening faster?

00:04:02.399 --> 00:04:05.183
Even just the idea of
something coming into my head

00:04:05.183 --> 00:04:07.996
of something that I want to do one day,

00:04:07.996 --> 00:04:10.373
I start taking action
on it, just naturally.

00:04:10.373 --> 00:04:12.816
If I wanted to build a house,

00:04:12.816 --> 00:04:15.606
I wanted to build a custom,
modern house from scratch

00:04:15.606 --> 00:04:17.666
and, like, yeah, that would
be good to do one day.

00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:19.921
Just having that thought in my head, boom!

00:04:19.921 --> 00:04:23.309
Within a year, I had my own
custom house being built.

00:04:23.309 --> 00:04:25.871
It just starts to happen
and I think getting used

00:04:25.871 --> 00:04:27.878
to taking action on your ideas

00:04:27.878 --> 00:04:29.730
is also really super important.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.685
Those plans that you have
for five or 10 years,

00:04:31.685 --> 00:04:34.001
they don't have to be five or 10 years.

00:04:34.001 --> 00:04:36.686
If you took action and started
doing stuff on it right now,

00:04:36.686 --> 00:04:39.711
you can make that happen
in five months or less,

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:43.417
maybe five weeks or five
days, for some of you,

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:45.472
if you actually started
taking action on it.

00:04:45.472 --> 00:04:46.964
And so, again, I think it's important

00:04:46.964 --> 00:04:49.440
to be stubborn about what
you want to accomplish,

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.406
'cause you're going to need it.

00:04:50.406 --> 00:04:51.618
You're going to need to be stubborn.

00:04:51.618 --> 00:04:55.410
You're going to need to face
criticism and face your fears

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.091
and get up every day and do action,

00:04:57.091 --> 00:04:59.347
but be flexible on the how

00:04:59.347 --> 00:05:00.771
and I would strongly encourage you,

00:05:00.771 --> 00:05:05.424
if you have a five-year goal
or a 10-year goal for yourself,

00:05:05.424 --> 00:05:06.851
raise your standards

00:05:06.851 --> 00:05:10.050
and start asking yourself how
do I hit that in five months?

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.145
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.711
what is your five- or 10-year goal

00:05:14.711 --> 00:05:17.684
that now you want to
condense down to five months?

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.839
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:05:18.839 --> 00:05:20.371
I'm really curious to find out and,

00:05:20.371 --> 00:05:22.080
if you leave a comment
within the first few hours

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.178
of this video going live,

00:05:23.178 --> 00:05:25.934
you have a chance to win
one of our two daily prizes.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:28.097
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Michael Pedersen.

00:05:28.097 --> 00:05:30.409
Michael, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:30.409 --> 00:05:31.475
Your One Word.

00:05:31.475 --> 00:05:32.469
I hope you enjoyed the read

00:05:32.469 --> 00:05:34.533
and it really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:35.911
Thank you, guys, again, for watching.

00:05:35.911 --> 00:05:37.094
I believe in you.

00:05:37.094 --> 00:05:38.900
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.781
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:40.781 --> 00:05:43.151
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:05:43.151 --> 00:05:45.692
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:45.692 --> 00:05:48.462
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:48.462 --> 00:05:52.080
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.014
(typewriter clicks)

00:05:55.014 --> 00:05:59.181
- I've had seasons where I've
had the worst surgeries ever.

00:06:01.551 --> 00:06:04.906
You know, I've been through,
I had seven surgeries.

00:06:04.906 --> 00:06:07.258
You know and that alone,

00:06:07.258 --> 00:06:09.184
you ask yourself time and time again,

00:06:09.184 --> 00:06:12.480
how do you bounce back from
that year in and year out?

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.108
But I've always used it as,
you know, taking that time

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.459
to strengthen myself.

00:06:16.459 --> 00:06:19.009
I never knew I was going to play 17 years.

00:06:19.009 --> 00:06:20.381
You know, who could've ever thought that?

00:06:20.381 --> 00:06:22.535
You don't say, when
you come into a league,

00:06:22.535 --> 00:06:24.651
you don't say, "You know what,
I'm going to play 17 years."

00:06:24.651 --> 00:06:25.895
And you don't even think of it that way.

00:06:25.895 --> 00:06:28.085
You just say I'll take it year by year.

00:06:28.085 --> 00:06:29.847
And that's what I try to tell kids.

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:32.655
Don't move to next year too fast.

00:06:32.655 --> 00:06:34.692
Just like don't go to tomorrow too fast.

00:06:34.692 --> 00:06:35.684
Deal with today.

00:06:35.684 --> 00:06:36.639
Deal with right now.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:37.746
You know, we've been in the locker room

00:06:37.746 --> 00:06:38.825
and we're at practice and I'm like,

00:06:38.825 --> 00:06:40.632
"Listen, put the phones down,

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:42.758
'cause these moments will go too fast."

00:06:42.758 --> 00:06:44.556
And when they're gone,
they're gone, you know?

00:06:44.556 --> 00:06:47.031
So, before you look up, you're
in two, three, five, seven,

00:06:47.031 --> 00:06:49.556
10, 12, if you make it that long.

00:06:49.556 --> 00:06:50.389
- Right.

00:06:50.389 --> 00:06:51.497
- Because most of them don't.

00:06:51.497 --> 00:06:52.946
You know, just like you
spoke about earlier.

00:06:52.946 --> 00:06:55.539
Most of these young babies
never see five years,

00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:58.810
never see seven years,
never less a 10-year career.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.635
You know, so you try to
prepare them to understand

00:07:01.635 --> 00:07:03.812
what the moment actually feels like

00:07:03.812 --> 00:07:05.740
and that's why I think, honestly,

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.748
why my career lasted so
long, 'cause I always lived

00:07:07.748 --> 00:07:08.828
in the moment.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:12.841
Like nothing else mattered to
me and I was selfish at times,

00:07:12.841 --> 00:07:16.301
because, even towards my
family, nothing else mattered

00:07:16.301 --> 00:07:17.998
when it came to that.

00:07:17.998 --> 00:07:20.098
When it came to that, I was dialed in.

00:07:20.098 --> 00:07:23.515
It's a heck of a blessing to be here now.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.353
I'm walking.

00:07:25.353 --> 00:07:27.103
I'm healthy, you see.

00:07:28.077 --> 00:07:29.045
- Still making an impact.

00:07:29.045 --> 00:07:30.021
- Absolutely.

00:07:30.021 --> 00:07:30.854
- Right.

00:07:30.854 --> 00:07:33.594
- Absolutely, so, you
know, I just tell people

00:07:33.594 --> 00:07:36.061
I don't know how long
whoever's going to play,

00:07:36.061 --> 00:07:38.394
but I will say enjoy every moment.

00:07:38.394 --> 00:07:39.741
Don't rush too fast.

00:07:39.741 --> 00:07:41.332
You know, let your years
take care of your years,

00:07:41.332 --> 00:07:44.080
but go year by year, go day
by day, go hour by hour,

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.254
go minute by minute.

00:07:45.254 --> 00:07:46.087
- A Head Full of Dreams.

00:07:46.087 --> 00:07:46.920
The tour's going on now.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.460
You just got off the South American line

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.293
- [Chris] Yeah.

00:07:49.293 --> 00:07:53.158
- I mean, the crowds,
the show, does it ever,

00:07:53.158 --> 00:07:56.413
how do you keep it fresh, because
it's not your first rodeo.

00:07:56.413 --> 00:07:58.496
It's your thousands, 10 thousands.

00:07:58.496 --> 00:07:59.941
I mean, you've been doing it.

00:07:59.941 --> 00:08:01.650
- Well, here's how we keep it fresh.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.204
Bruce Springsteen, apparently,

00:08:03.204 --> 00:08:04.521
I don't know if he really does or not,

00:08:04.521 --> 00:08:07.500
used to say to the rest
of the E Street Band,

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.076
this could be someone's first show

00:08:09.076 --> 00:08:10.412
and it could be someone's last show,

00:08:10.412 --> 00:08:12.389
so let's treat it like that.

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:15.847
So, I have that inspiration
and then some other things

00:08:15.847 --> 00:08:17.751
in my life that just make me,

00:08:17.751 --> 00:08:19.131
but every time before we go on stage,

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.008
I really think about who's showed up,

00:08:21.008 --> 00:08:22.833
how much they've been
through to get there.

00:08:22.833 --> 00:08:23.666
- [Zach] Wow.

00:08:23.666 --> 00:08:27.447
- And also for us, at the
moment, we took a break

00:08:27.447 --> 00:08:29.809
from touring on the last album
we did called Ghost Stories,

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:32.757
so we're so excited to be there

00:08:32.757 --> 00:08:34.789
and we know that nothing lasts forever,

00:08:34.789 --> 00:08:36.727
so I think that we're just
really, more than ever,

00:08:36.727 --> 00:08:40.032
living in the moment and
trying to appreciate the fact

00:08:40.032 --> 00:08:41.908
that for some people it's their first show

00:08:41.908 --> 00:08:43.439
and some people, you know.
- [Zach] Yeah.

00:08:43.439 --> 00:08:45.767
That has to be a perspective
that that's not immediate,

00:08:45.767 --> 00:08:46.600
right?

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.433
You learn that perspective.
- We have to work

00:08:47.433 --> 00:08:48.266
to that perspective.

00:08:48.266 --> 00:08:49.099
- [Zach] Yeah.

00:08:49.099 --> 00:08:50.572
- We definitely went through
a period about 10 years ago

00:08:50.572 --> 00:08:52.399
of feeling like what are we doing?

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:54.918
You know, we're questioning
everything and not really able

00:08:54.918 --> 00:08:56.742
to take in the joy of it.

00:08:56.742 --> 00:08:58.056
- [Zach] That's must've been hard.

00:08:58.056 --> 00:09:01.605
- Well, everything's in
perspective, but, for us as a band,

00:09:01.605 --> 00:09:03.105
it was a bit hard.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:07.030
But slowly, you just keep going
and you find great people,

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:10.215
who come in and help you
out and teach you things.

00:09:10.215 --> 00:09:12.611
And I think the more that you let in,

00:09:12.611 --> 00:09:15.120
it's very easy right now with social media

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.012
to let in anything negative, you know.

00:09:17.012 --> 00:09:19.990
Whatever you do, someone is
going to slag it off online.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.737
- Well, you're not on social media at all.

00:09:21.737 --> 00:09:22.570
- [Chris] Personally.

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:23.403
I mean, we are as a band.

00:09:23.403 --> 00:09:24.236
- As a band.

00:09:24.236 --> 00:09:26.240
Personally, I'm not that good at selfies.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.278
(everyone laughs)

00:09:27.278 --> 00:09:29.511
- That's the honest answer.

00:09:29.511 --> 00:09:32.570
- So I made a decision that,

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.536
well, it's easy to take in the bad stuff,

00:09:34.536 --> 00:09:37.705
so I'm going to really take in
the good stuff and appreciate.

00:09:37.705 --> 00:09:38.883
These people have shown up

00:09:38.883 --> 00:09:42.375
and they want to sing our songs
together and that's great.

00:09:42.375 --> 00:09:43.982
I'm into it. (laughs)

00:09:43.982 --> 00:09:45.192
- [Zach] It can't ever get old.

00:09:45.192 --> 00:09:46.025
- So, it's very fresh.

00:09:46.025 --> 00:09:47.068
It never gets old, that's the thing.

00:09:47.068 --> 00:09:48.318
It never gets old.

00:09:48.318 --> 00:09:50.568
- Funny thing about gigs is

00:09:51.905 --> 00:09:54.159
there are so many factors
that make a great gig.

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.815
Like, I've come off stage so many times,

00:09:56.815 --> 00:10:00.244
thinking that was awful,
for whatever reason.

00:10:00.244 --> 00:10:02.362
You know, your sound man will
come in that was out front

00:10:02.362 --> 00:10:04.026
and say, "That's the best
thing I've ever seen."

00:10:04.026 --> 00:10:05.091
You go, "Really?!"

00:10:05.091 --> 00:10:06.010
(interviewer laughs)

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.093
Or then you'll be off stage

00:10:07.093 --> 00:10:11.948
and think that your band has
played great and you've really

00:10:11.948 --> 00:10:14.013
and the sound man will come in
and say, "Oh, I lost the bass

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:15.089
for six songs."

00:10:15.089 --> 00:10:16.331
And you're like, "Really?!"

00:10:16.331 --> 00:10:17.164
Or the lighting man will say,

00:10:17.164 --> 00:10:18.170
"Yes, well, the lights didn't work."

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:19.095
So, you know what I mean?

00:10:19.095 --> 00:10:22.629
It's kind of, I don't really judge gigs.

00:10:22.629 --> 00:10:24.284
While I'm doing it, I'm just in the moment

00:10:24.284 --> 00:10:25.849
and I'm singing the songs
and when I come off stage,

00:10:25.849 --> 00:10:27.051
I don't like talking about it.

